// Original instructional contexts. Source lists select headwords only; these are not official SAT items.
const SOURCE_EXPANSION_3_EXTRA={
resisted:'opposed or refused to comply',equivocated:'spoke evasively',objected:'expressed opposition',
separation:'division into distinct parts',scarcity:'insufficient supply',replacement:'substitution of one thing for another',
expansion:'increase in extent',restoration:'return to a former condition',stability:'absence of significant change',
inhibited:'restrained or slowed',concealing:'hiding from view',replicating:'making another instance of',
rejected:'refused to accept',confirmed:'established as accurate',resolved:'settled or solved',
'argued with':'disputed a position with someone','ignored':'gave no attention to','interviewed':'asked someone questions',
conceals:'hides or makes less visible',contradicts:'conflicts with a statement',necessitates:'makes necessary',
concentrated:'gathered closely together',standardized:'made uniform',authenticated:'verified as genuine',
detachment:'absence of emotional involvement',disagreement:'difference of opinion',interruption:'break in a continuing activity',
'causes of':'things that produce an effect','remedies for':'means of correcting a problem','barriers to':'things that obstruct an activity',
'isolated from':'kept apart from','substituted for':'put in place of','modeled on':'designed after an example',
exclusively:'solely or only',partially:'to some extent',conditionally:'subject to a requirement',
restriction:'limitation on action',uniformity:'sameness among parts',precision:'exactness or accuracy',
disguising:'concealing the nature of',discarding:'getting rid of',exaggerating:'making something appear greater',
agreement:'shared acceptance of a position',gratitude:'appreciation for a benefit',prediction:'statement about a future event',
obsolete:'no longer useful or current',imminent:'about to happen',cumulative:'increasing through successive additions',
intermittent:'occurring at irregular intervals',accidental:'happening without intention',continuous:'without interruption',
advocates:'people supporting a position',opponents:'people opposing a position',beneficiaries:'people receiving an advantage',observers:'people watching events',
original:'the first or authentic instance',obstacle:'something that impedes progress',surplus:'more than is needed',
reconciliation:'restoration of friendly relations',compensation:'payment for loss or damage',disclosure:'making information known',
predecessor:'someone or something that came before',simultaneity:'occurrence at the same time',stagnation:'lack of development or movement',
fabrication:'invention presented as fact',evasion:'avoidance of a question or responsibility',
'dependence on':'reliance on something','aversion to':'strong dislike of something','awareness of':'knowledge of something',
justified:'supported by sufficient reasons',prohibited:'forbidden',anticipated:'expected beforehand',
'summarize (in)':'give a brief overview in a stated form','object (to)':'express opposition to something','comply (with)':'act according to a requirement'
};
const SOURCE_EXPANSION_3=[];
function add3(word,meaning,cue,distractors,a,ca,b,cb){SOURCE_EXPANSION_3.push([word,meaning,'Memory cue: '+cue,distractors,a,ca,b,cb]);}
add3('abound','exist in large numbers','abundant examples abound.','diminish,disappear,fluctuate','Examples of the motif _____ throughout the collection: researchers found it in nearly every manuscript, often several times on a single page. It is therefore far from rare within this archive.','Nearly every manuscript and repeated instances establish plentiful occurrence; fluctuate would require changing amounts.','Detailed descriptions of river travel _____ in the memoir, appearing in almost every chapter. Readers encounter far more examples than they would need to establish the author’s sustained interest in navigation.','Repeated plentiful examples support abound; diminish would indicate decreasing numbers.');
add3('acquiesced','accepted or complied without protest','quiet compliance can coexist with dislike.','resisted,equivocated,objected','The editor privately preferred the earlier title but allowed the publisher’s replacement without complaint or challenge. She _____ despite her reservations, accepting the change rather than trying to reverse it.','Acceptance without protest fits; resisted would mean opposition.','Although dissatisfied with the new schedule, the researcher _____ when the committee approved it. He followed the arrangement without objection and made no attempt to reopen the decision.','Following without objection establishes compliance; equivocated would mean evasive speech.');
add3('aggregation','collection or combination of separate items','an aggregate gathers pieces together.','separation,scarcity,replacement','Each institution supplied its own records, and the investigators combined them into one dataset. This _____ enabled comparisons that no individual institution’s smaller collection could support on its own.','Combination of separate collections establishes aggregation; separation would divide them.','The report presents an _____ of local counts into a regional total, adding the figures from every district. It retains the original tables so readers can inspect the components of the sum.','Adding counts into a total indicates combination; replacement would substitute one thing for another.');
add3('ambiguous','open to more than one interpretation','two reasonable readings signal ambiguity.','explicit,irrelevant,unequivocal','The instruction could mean either that all specimens must be tested twice or that only failed specimens need another test. Its _____ wording left technicians unsure which procedure the authors intended.','Two plausible readings establish ambiguity; explicit would clearly state the requirement.','The critic called the performance unusual but gave no clue whether that observation expressed approval or disapproval. Her _____ comment permitted both favorable and unfavorable interpretations among readers of the review.','Opposite possible interpretations establish ambiguity; unequivocal would rule them out.');
add3('ample','more than enough for a purpose','ample supplies leave room to spare.','negligible,sporadic,nonexistent','The grant covered every planned expense and left a substantial reserve for unforeseen repairs. The archive therefore had _____ funds for completing the restoration, rather than merely enough to begin it.','Full costs plus reserve show sufficiency with room to spare; negligible would mean insignificant.','Researchers had _____ time to inspect the collection: their visit lasted three weeks, while the complete examination required only four days. They could repeat checks without delaying their return.','Available time greatly exceeds required time; sporadic describes irregular occurrence.');
add3('annihilate','destroy completely','annihilation leaves none of the target intact.','augment,attenuate,corroborate','The proposed treatment would _____ the colony, leaving no living members rather than merely reducing its population. Conservation staff rejected that outcome because maintaining some organisms was essential to their study.','No living members indicates complete destruction; attenuate would merely weaken.','In the simulation, the impact would _____ the entire settlement, with no building or infrastructure left standing. The prediction concerns total destruction, not the limited damage associated with smaller collisions.','Nothing remains standing, establishing total destruction; augment would increase.');
add3('apparent','seeming true from initial appearances','an apparent pattern may disappear after checking.','substantiated,immutable,irrelevant','An _____ difference between the groups disappeared when researchers corrected a labeling error. What first looked like a genuine contrast had been an artifact rather than a demonstrated feature of the data.','Initial appearance proves misleading; substantiated would imply evidentiary support.','The building’s _____ symmetry proved illusory: measurements revealed unequal wings concealed by the facade. Visitors’ first impressions therefore differed from the structure established by the architect’s precise survey.','Seeming symmetry is disproved by measurements; immutable would mean incapable of change.');
add3('ascribe','attribute something to a cause or source','ascribe credit by naming its source.','obscure,eliminate,substantiate','Without claiming that weather explained every change, the researchers _____ the sudden decline to an unusually severe drought. Their account identifies the drought as the principal cause of this particular decrease.','Naming a cause establishes attribution; substantiate would support a claim with evidence.','The catalog editors _____ the unsigned painting to a particular workshop, identifying that studio as its likely source. They distinguish this attribution from certainty about which individual artist applied the paint.','Assigning the painting a source means attribute; obscure would hide the source.');
add3('attrition','gradual reduction through repeated losses','small losses accumulate into attrition.','expansion,restoration,stability','The group began with fifty volunteers, but a few withdrew each month until only twenty remained. This _____ reduced participation gradually rather than through one sudden decision to dissolve the organization.','Repeated withdrawals establish gradual loss; expansion would mean growth.','Constant use wore away small portions of the surface year after year. The resulting _____ eventually reduced the object’s size noticeably, even though no single episode caused dramatic damage.','Accumulated wear indicates gradual reduction; restoration would reverse loss.');
add3('autonomous','able to govern or operate independently','autonomy means making one’s own decisions.','contingent,reciprocal,provisional','The regional council sets its own policies and budget without seeking approval from the national organization. It is _____ in these matters, retaining decision-making authority despite maintaining cooperative relationships elsewhere.','Independent decisions establish autonomy; reciprocal would mean mutual exchange.','Once activated, the device chooses routes and adjusts its behavior without further instructions from operators. Its _____ operation contrasts with earlier models that required a human to direct every movement.','Operation without continuing direction indicates independence; provisional means temporary or unconfirmed.');
add3('byzantine','excessively intricate or complicated','imagine a maze of procedural turns.','succinct,coherent,prosaic','Obtaining approval requires fifteen overlapping forms, several circular referrals, and signatures from offices with conflicting jurisdictions. Applicants describe the process as _____ because its convoluted procedures are unusually difficult to navigate.','Overlapping circular procedures establish excessive complexity; coherent would mean consistently connected.','The treaty’s exceptions refer to other exceptions that redirect readers to still more qualifications. Its _____ structure obscures basic obligations beneath a maze of clauses, making straightforward application extraordinarily difficult.','Maze of interdependent clauses indicates intricate complexity; succinct would mean brief and clear.');
add3('capitulate','surrender or give in to demands','capitulation ends resistance.','equivocate,assert,elaborate','After months of resisting the requested changes, the director agreed to every condition imposed by the funders. She decided to _____ rather than continue opposition that could cost the institution its support.','Giving in to conditions after resistance establishes capitulation; equivocate would avoid a clear position.','The negotiator initially rejected the ultimatum but ultimately chose to _____, accepting the entire package without securing any concession. His final position abandoned the resistance maintained during earlier discussions.','Acceptance without concessions ends resistance; assert would state a position, not surrender.');
add3('catalyzing','causing or accelerating a development','a catalyst helps a change get underway.','concealing,replicating,inhibiting','By bringing previously isolated researchers together, the workshop was _____ new collaborations: projects began immediately afterward that participants said would not otherwise have occurred. Its effect went beyond simply displaying existing partnerships.','New projects prompted by the workshop establish stimulation; replicating would repeat existing collaborations.','The inexpensive instrument was _____ a surge of research, enabling laboratories previously unable to make the measurements to start new studies. Publication rates increased sharply after its introduction across the field.','Instrument enables and prompts research growth; inhibiting would slow it.');
add3('clandestine','kept secret, especially because unauthorized','clandestine meetings stay out of public view.','explicit,ubiquitous,perfunctory','The participants used coded messages and met after closing hours so officials would not discover their unauthorized negotiations. These _____ discussions were deliberately concealed rather than merely omitted from an ordinary public schedule.','Concealment of unauthorized negotiations establishes secrecy; explicit would mean openly expressed.','The expedition entered the restricted site at night and withheld its plans from the authorities. Its _____ preparations aimed to prevent discovery of an undertaking that had received no official permission.','Intentional concealment of unauthorized activity fits; perfunctory describes superficial effort.');
add3('complicate','make more difficult or complex','additional interacting factors complicate a problem.','elucidate,obviate,corroborate','The new evidence introduces two plausible causes where researchers had previously assumed only one. These alternatives _____ the analysis by requiring additional comparisons before the observed effect can be assigned to a source.','Additional possibilities increase analytical difficulty; elucidate would clarify.','Conflicting ownership claims _____ the proposed donation, forcing the museum to resolve legal questions before accepting the object. Without those claims, the transfer would have required only a routine agreement.','New legal questions make transfer more difficult; obviate would make something unnecessary.');
add3('confounded','perplexed or bewildered','confounding results leave an observer puzzled.','confirmed,resolved,rejected','Every measurement contradicted the engineer’s expectations, yet no instrument error could be found. _____ by the unexplained pattern, she admitted that she could not yet understand how the system behaved.','Admitted inability to understand indicates perplexity; confirmed would mean established as accurate.','The critic was _____ by the novel’s shifting chronology, unable to determine which events preceded the others. Repeated reading increased her uncertainty rather than resolving the puzzling arrangement of scenes.','Unresolved puzzlement supports bewildered; resolved would suggest uncertainty had ended.');
add3('conspicuous','readily noticeable','conspicuous features catch the eye.','implicit,negligible,esoteric','A bright red square occupies the center of the otherwise gray canvas. This _____ feature immediately attracts viewers’ attention, even when they are standing too far away to inspect small details.','Immediate visual attention establishes noticeability; implicit means indirectly conveyed.','The corrected date appears in large type at the top of the notice. Its _____ placement makes it difficult to overlook, unlike the earlier correction buried among dense footnotes.','Prominent placement establishes noticeability; esoteric would concern specialist knowledge.');
add3('continuity','unbroken connection or persistence','continuity keeps the thread intact.','interruption,disagreement,detachment','Although different editors supervised successive volumes, each preserved the same methods and organization. This _____ linked the entire series, allowing readers to follow one consistent approach across decades of publication.','Consistent approach across changing editors indicates connection; interruption would break it.','The records show that the practice persisted without a gap from the earliest documented period to the present. This _____ challenges the claim that it vanished and was later reinvented.','Persistence without a gap establishes continuity; interruption contradicts it.');
add3('convergence','coming together toward a shared point or result','converging paths approach one another.','separation,scarcity,replacement','Independent research teams initially proposed very different estimates, but improved measurements brought their results progressively closer. This _____ culminated in nearly identical values despite the teams’ distinct analytical methods.','Increasing agreement establishes coming together; separation would mean moving apart.','The two artistic traditions began with contrasting methods, yet later works increasingly shared techniques and visual conventions. Their _____ reflects growing similarity rather than the replacement of one tradition by the other.','Increasing similarity means coming together; replacement is explicitly excluded.');
add3('counterintuitive','contrary to what one would initially expect','counterintuitive results reverse a first prediction.','inevitable,analogous,irrelevant','Reducing the number of available choices increased participants’ satisfaction, contrary to their stated expectation that more options would help. Researchers described this outcome as _____ because it reversed that natural prediction.','Reversal of initial expectation fits; inevitable concerns certainty.','The thicker material transmitted more light than the thinner sample, even though observers expected greater thickness to block it. This _____ finding required an explanation of the material’s unusual internal structure.','Opposition to expected effect establishes counterintuitive; analogous means similar in a relevant respect.');
add3('decisive','settling an issue conclusively','decisive evidence ends the relevant uncertainty.','tentative,equivocal,irrelevant','The authenticated letter explicitly dates the event and excludes every competing chronology. It supplies _____ evidence for the timing question, resolving a dispute that earlier indirect clues could not settle.','Excluding alternatives settles the issue; equivocal would leave different readings possible.','The final experiment distinguished the two hypotheses because only one predicted the observed result. Its _____ outcome settled which explanation fit the tested conditions, ending the uncertainty left by previous trials.','Distinguishing hypotheses resolves the issue; tentative would remain provisional.');
add3('deferred to','accepted another’s judgment or authority','defer to expertise by letting it guide the decision.','argued with,ignored,interviewed','Recognizing her superior knowledge of the damaged instrument, the committee _____ the engineer and adopted her recommendation without modification. Members allowed her technical judgment to determine their final choice.','Adopting her judgment establishes deference; interviewed would mean merely asking questions.','The editor _____ the linguist on the disputed translation, setting aside his own preference and using the specialist’s wording. Her expertise, rather than his initial intuition, governed the final version.','Setting aside own judgment for expert establishes deference; argued with would imply dispute.');
add3('denotes','indicates or stands for','a symbol denotes what it represents.','conceals,contradicts,necessitates','In this diagram, a filled circle _____ an occupied site, while an empty circle represents a vacant one. The legend assigns each symbol a meaning rather than describing what causes occupancy.','Symbol represents occupancy; necessitates would claim it makes occupancy required.','The abbreviation _____ a unit of distance, not a particular measurement technique. Readers can interpret the table correctly by replacing it with the unit’s full name wherever it appears.','Abbreviation stands for unit; conceals would hide the meaning.');
add3('discerning','showing perceptive judgment about distinctions','discerning readers notice meaningful differences.','indifferent,perfunctory,arbitrary','The critic distinguishes subtle variations in rhythm that other readers overlook, explaining how each changes the poem’s effect. Her _____ analysis reflects perceptive judgment rather than merely an accumulation of examples.','Noticing meaningful subtle distinctions indicates perception; perfunctory would be superficial.','The curator’s _____ eye identifies small but consequential differences among otherwise similar objects. She explains which details establish authenticity instead of treating every visible irregularity as equally important to attribution.','Judgment distinguishes consequential details; arbitrary would lack a consistent reason.');
add3('dispersed','spread out over an area','dispersed objects are scattered apart.','concentrated,standardized,authenticated','Instead of forming one dense cluster, the settlements were _____ across a broad valley, separated by several kilometers. Mapping their distribution required surveying the entire region rather than one compact site.','Wide separation indicates spreading; concentrated would mean closely grouped.','The fragments were _____ through several layers and distant sections of the excavation. Their scattered locations contrasted with intact objects recovered together from a single storage chamber near the entrance.','Scattered locations establish dispersal; authenticated concerns verified genuineness.');
add3('earnest','serious and sincerely committed','earnest appeals mean what they say.','jocular,disingenuous,indifferent','The appeal contains no jokes or calculated flattery; its author expresses genuine concern and sustained commitment to helping affected residents. Its _____ tone reflects serious purpose rather than performative enthusiasm.','Serious genuine concern establishes earnest; disingenuous would suggest insincerity.','The student’s questions were _____, motivated by a sincere desire to understand rather than an attempt to amuse classmates. She listened carefully and returned to points she had not grasped.','Sincere serious learning fits; jocular would indicate humor.');
add3('efface','erase or make no longer visible','effacing a mark removes its visible trace.','augment,substantiate,elucidate','The restoration team will _____ the later pencil marks without altering the original ink. Their objective is to remove those additions entirely so the earlier writing is no longer obscured.','Removing visible marks entirely establishes erasure; elucidate means make clear through explanation.','Repeated polishing can _____ the engraved inscription, eventually leaving a smooth surface with no legible trace. Conservators therefore avoid treatment that would erase the lettering they are trying to preserve.','No trace remains after polishing; augment would increase the inscription.');
add3('elide','omit or leave out','an elided step disappears from the account.','elaborate,corroborate,augment','To keep the summary brief, the editor chose to _____ the intermediate calculations and present only the initial assumptions and final result. The complete working remained available in a separate appendix.','Leaving calculations out establishes omission; elaborate would add detail.','The biography tends to _____ the author’s unsuccessful experiments, moving directly from early ambitions to celebrated achievements. Readers seeking those omitted episodes must consult records outside the published narrative.','Unsuccessful episodes are omitted; corroborate would support them with evidence.');
add3('emanate','issue or originate from a source','emanating signals come out from somewhere.','converge,disappear,fluctuate','The signals _____ from a single transmitter, spreading outward toward receivers located throughout the valley. Mapping their direction allowed technicians to identify that device as the origin of the emissions.','Outward signals originate at transmitter; converge would move toward a common point.','The disagreements _____ from incompatible definitions of the central term, not from conflicting observations. Once the researchers identified that source, they could explain why identical data had led to different claims.','Definitions are identified as source; disappear would mean cease to exist.');
add3('endearing','inspiring affection','endearing quirks make people feel fond.','inimical,irrelevant,perfunctory','The character’s awkward attempts to help others make readers fond of him despite his mistakes. Critics describe these gestures as _____ because their imperfect kindness inspires affection rather than ridicule.','Imperfect kindness inspires fondness; inimical would mean hostile or harmful.','The artist’s habit of thanking every assistant by name was _____ to colleagues, who responded with genuine warmth. They valued this personal kindness beyond its practical role in organizing work.','Warm affection establishes endearing; perfunctory would imply superficial routine attention.');
add3('entice','attract or persuade with something appealing','enticing offers draw people in.','repudiate,preclude,obscure','The organizers hope to _____ reluctant visitors with demonstrations and free access to the collection. These appealing incentives are intended to draw people into an exhibition they might otherwise skip.','Appealing incentives attract participation; preclude would prevent it.','To _____ researchers into examining the neglected archive, the foundation offers travel grants and digitization support. The benefits are designed to make participation attractive rather than impose an obligation.','Attractive benefits encourage participation; obscure would make something less clear.');
add3('exact','demand and obtain; impose a cost','exact payment by requiring it.','waive,refund,subsidize','The agency can _____ payment from every operator as a condition of renewing a license. Its rules require the fee in full rather than allowing applicants to retain that money.','Required payment is demanded and obtained; waive would cancel it.','The demanding schedule will _____ a substantial toll on the team’s energy, requiring long hours with little rest. Organizers expect fatigue as a direct cost of completing the work so quickly.','Schedule imposes an energy cost; subsidize would provide support rather than impose a toll.');
add3('exploit','make effective use of; take unfair advantage of','context distinguishes useful application from unfair advantage.','obviate,preclude,repudiate','The researchers _____ the instrument’s unusually high resolution to detect structures invisible in earlier images. They use this capability deliberately, obtaining information that ordinary equipment cannot provide at the same scale.','Effective use of capability fits; preclude would prevent access.','The employers _____ workers by withholding promised wages while demanding extra hours, unfairly taking advantage of their limited bargaining power. The report describes mistreatment rather than mutually beneficial use of available skills.','Withholding deserved pay establishes unfair advantage; repudiate would mean reject or disavow rather than mistreat.');
add3('expound (on)','explain a topic systematically or in detail','expounding goes beyond a brief mention.','summarize (in),object (to),comply (with)','A usage guide groups verbs by purpose and lists entries with their usual prepositions in parentheses. Its entry _____ belongs under detailed explanation, illustrated by a lecturer systematically developing a theory.','Detailed systematic explanation identifies expound; summarize would give a brief overview.','An editor needs a dictionary entry for explaining a subject at length, not opposing it or following instructions. In notation that places the usual preposition in parentheses, the appropriate entry is _____.','Explaining at length fits expound; object means express opposition.');
add3('extrapolate','estimate beyond known data by extending a pattern','extrapolation carries a measured trend beyond its range.','interpolate,replicate,obscure','The study measures growth through age ten, but the analyst tries to _____ later values by extending the observed trend. Those estimates lie beyond the ages for which direct measurements are available.','Extending beyond measured range establishes extrapolation; interpolate estimates within that range.','Using records from the first five years, the model will _____ demand for the following decade. Its projections extend an existing pattern rather than report observations actually collected during those future years.','Future projection extends known pattern; replicate would repeat an instance.');
add3('fiscal','relating to government revenue and spending','fiscal policy concerns public budgets.','linguistic,botanical,geometric','The report examines tax receipts, public borrowing, and government spending rather than interest-rate decisions. Its _____ focus centers on the state’s budget and how revenues support planned expenditures.','Public revenue and spending define fiscal; linguistic would concern language.','The council’s _____ responsibilities include approving the municipal budget and deciding how local tax income is allocated. They concern public finances rather than the design or administration of individual buildings.','Budget and tax allocation establish public finance; geometric concerns shape.');
add3('foster','encourage the growth or development of','fostering creates conditions for growth.','inhibit,preclude,repudiate','The program provides mentoring, equipment, and opportunities for collaboration to _____ early-career research. Its aim is to support development, not dictate which conclusions participants must ultimately reach in their studies.','Support encourages development; inhibit would hinder it.','Open discussion and accessible records can _____ trust among collaborators, helping a cooperative relationship develop over time. The measures are intended to cultivate confidence rather than merely announce that it exists.','Cultivating trust establishes encouragement; preclude would prevent it.');
add3('habituate','make accustomed through repeated exposure','habits form as repeated experiences become familiar.','startle,sensitize,exclude','Repeated gentle handling can _____ the animals to human presence, making them less reactive over time. The procedure aims to establish familiarity rather than intensify their response to each approach.','Repeated exposure reduces reaction through familiarity; sensitize would increase responsiveness.','Daily practice sessions _____ participants to background noise, which gradually becomes less distracting. Researchers attribute the change to repeated experience rather than improvements in the room’s soundproofing or equipment.','Noise becomes familiar with repetition; startle would cause sudden alarm.');
add3('harbinger','an early sign of something to come','a harbinger announces what may follow.','aftermath,remedy,obstacle','The first decline in bookings proved a _____ of the broader downturn that followed months later. Analysts now regard it as an early warning, not a consequence of the later contraction.','Early warning before downturn fits; aftermath would follow it.','The newly observed behavior may be a _____ of a larger ecological shift, appearing before other changes become measurable. Researchers will monitor whether the expected developments follow this initial signal.','Signal precedes possible development; remedy would address a problem.');
add3('hypothesize','propose a possible explanation for testing','hypotheses invite investigation rather than assume proof.','verify,refute,eliminate','The researchers _____ that soil chemistry accounts for the unexpected pattern, but have not measured the relevant compounds. Their proposal supplies a testable explanation rather than an established finding.','Untested proposed explanation fits; verify would require checking and confirming.','Before gathering additional evidence, the team will _____ a mechanism that could explain the observations. It will then design experiments capable of distinguishing that proposal from plausible alternatives.','Proposal before testing establishes hypothesize; refute would disprove a claim.');
add3('illuminate','make clearer or easier to understand','illumination brings a difficult issue into clearer view.','obscure,complicate,repudiate','The newly discovered diary can _____ the dispute by explaining why each side rejected the same proposal. It supplies motives missing from the official record, making the disagreement easier to understand.','Missing motives clarify dispute; complicate would increase difficulty.','The teacher uses a concrete example to _____ the abstract principle, connecting unfamiliar notation with a situation students already understand. The explanation makes the idea clearer without changing its meaning.','Familiar example clarifies principle; obscure would make it less clear.');
add3('immoderate','excessive or beyond reasonable limits','immoderate demands go too far.','negligible,circumspect,commensurate','The sponsor demanded twenty additional studies within a week, far beyond what the staff could reasonably complete. The director rejected these _____ expectations as excessive given the available time and resources.','Demands exceed reasonable capacity; commensurate would be proportional to resources.','The critic’s _____ praise attributed perfection to every paragraph and denied even obvious weaknesses. Readers found the enthusiasm excessive, much greater than the work’s actual accomplishments could reasonably justify.','Excessive disproportionate praise fits; circumspect would be cautious.');
add3('imperative','urgently necessary','imperative steps cannot responsibly be postponed.','superfluous,optional,irrelevant','Because untreated damage was spreading rapidly, immediate stabilization was _____. Conservators could not safely postpone it until the routine restoration cycle without risking the loss of irreplaceable material.','Urgent necessity rules out optional; superfluous would mean unnecessary.','It is _____ to verify the specimen before using it in the trial, since a mistaken identification would invalidate every result. This requirement is essential rather than a discretionary enhancement of the procedure.','Results require verification, making it necessary; optional contradicts that requirement.');
add3('implausible','difficult to believe or unlikely to be reasonable','implausible explanations strain what the evidence permits.','substantiated,tenable,unequivocal','The proposed journey would require a traveler to cover distances far beyond any documented capability in the available time. Historians regard this account as _____, though missing records prevent definitive disproof.','Required speed makes account hard to believe; substantiated would imply evidentiary support.','The mechanism depends on temperatures that the site almost never experiences and materials absent from all tested samples. Researchers therefore consider it an _____ explanation of the ordinary conditions observed there.','Mechanism poorly matches conditions; tenable would mean defensible.');
add3('inane','empty of sense or substance','inane remarks offer nothing sensible.','cogent,nuanced,pertinent','The speaker’s repeated assertion that things happen because they happen supplied no explanation at all. Listeners called the remark _____, noting its emptiness rather than any difficulty in understanding its words.','Circular empty remark lacks substance; cogent would mean convincingly reasoned.','The commentary replaced analysis with meaningless slogans that addressed none of the evidence. Its _____ observations contributed no sensible account of the problem, despite occupying several pages of the published report.','Meaningless slogans lack substance; pertinent would directly address the issue.');
add3('incongruence','lack of fit or consistency between things','incongruence means pieces do not fit together.','agreement,continuity,uniformity','The solemn narration accompanies cheerful comic music, producing an _____ between tone and accompaniment. Reviewers emphasize their mismatch, not a lack of quality in either element considered by itself.','Clashing elements establish mismatch; agreement would suggest fit.','The institution proclaims openness while barring access to records it promised to release. This _____ between stated principles and actual practices raises questions about the consistency of its public commitments.','Practice conflicts with principle; continuity concerns persistence rather than mismatch.');
add3('incremental','occurring through small successive additions','increments build change step by step.','abrupt,immutable,sporadic','Rather than replace the system overnight, technicians introduced one small improvement each month. Their _____ approach accumulated changes gradually while allowing the facility to continue operating throughout the transition.','Small successive improvements fit; abrupt would mean sudden.','The model’s accuracy improved through many minor adjustments, each adding a little to previous gains. Researchers describe this _____ progress as cumulative rather than the product of one dramatic breakthrough.','Successive small gains establish incremental; sporadic concerns irregular occurrence.');
add3('indices of','indicators or signs of something','indices point toward a condition.','causes of,remedies for,barriers to','The survey treats abandoned storefronts as _____ economic decline, using them to detect a condition already developing. It does not claim that empty shops initiate or remedy the broader downturn.','Used as signs rather than causes; causes of is explicitly excluded.','Changes in leaf color serve as _____ nutrient deficiency, helping researchers recognize the underlying problem. The color changes are observed consequences, not interventions that correct the shortage in the soil.','Observed signs indicate deficiency; remedies for would correct it.');
add3('induce','cause or bring about','induced effects result from an intervention.','preclude,obviate,corroborate','The altered lighting can _____ flowering in plants that would otherwise remain dormant under these conditions. Controlled trials show that the change initiates the process rather than merely accompanying it.','Lighting initiates flowering, establishing causation; corroborate would supply support for a claim.','Researchers apply the stimulus to _____ a measurable response, which begins immediately afterward in treated samples but not controls. The procedure deliberately brings about the change under investigation.','Stimulus brings about response; preclude would prevent it.');
add3('intermingled with','mixed together with','intermingling places different kinds among one another.','isolated from,substituted for,modeled on','Organic fibers were _____ mineral particles throughout the specimen, with neither material confined to a separate layer. Their mixed distribution required researchers to analyze several components within every section.','Mixed distribution supports intermingling; isolated from would mean separation.','In the anthology, personal recollections are _____ official documents, appearing among them rather than in a distinct section. Readers encounter both kinds repeatedly as they proceed through the volume.','Alternating among each other establishes mixing; substituted for would mean replacement.');
add3('irrespective','without regard to a factor','irrespective of means the factor does not change the outcome.','exclusively,partially,conditionally','The prize is open to every eligible researcher, _____ of nationality. Applicants from all countries are judged by the same criteria, and citizenship neither grants an advantage nor excludes participation.','Nationality has no effect; exclusively would imply limitation.','The instrument records all events above the threshold, _____ of their duration. Short and long events are included alike whenever they meet the specified intensity requirement for detection.','Duration makes no difference; conditionally would imply dependence on that factor.');
add3('latitude','freedom to act; angular distance north or south of the equator','context distinguishes room to maneuver from a geographic coordinate.','restriction,uniformity,precision','Within broad ethical rules, the grant gives researchers considerable _____ to choose methods and topics. They can revise their plans without obtaining permission for every individual decision during the project.','Independent choices establish freedom; restriction would limit them.','The map lists the station’s _____ as fifty-two degrees north, specifying its angular position relative to the equator. This coordinate describes geographic location rather than how freely the staff may conduct research.','Degrees north of the equator establish geographic latitude; precision describes accuracy, not the coordinate itself.');
add3('maudlin','excessively or weakly sentimental','maudlin emotion overwhelms proportion.','dispassionate,prosaic,nuanced','The tribute dwells on tears and idealized memories, portraying its subject without any flaws or complexity. Critics find it _____, arguing that excessive sentiment replaces a balanced understanding of the person.','Excessive idealized sentiment fits; nuanced would preserve complexity.','Rather than explore loss with restraint, the scene repeatedly demands tears through exaggerated declarations and implausibly perfect recollections. Its _____ treatment turns emotion into sentimental excess instead of careful characterization.','Sentimental excess establishes maudlin; dispassionate would lack emotional involvement.');
add3('modesty','absence of boastfulness or exaggerated self-importance','modesty credits others without self-advertisement.','arrogance,hostility,evasion','The researcher acknowledged collaborators and avoided presenting herself as the sole source of success. Her _____ reflected an unpretentious assessment of contributions, not uncertainty about the quality of the work.','Unboastful shared credit establishes modesty; evasion would avoid a question.','Though widely celebrated, the performer discussed achievements without self-promotion and readily praised colleagues. Reviewers noted her _____, contrasting it with the grand claims some artists made about their own importance.','No self-promotion fits modesty; arrogance implies exaggerated importance.');
add3('monetizing','turning something into a source of revenue','monetizing makes access or use produce income.','disguising,discarding,exaggerating','The company is _____ its archive by charging institutions for licensed access to digitized records. Material once offered free now produces revenue through subscriptions and fees for authorized reuse.','Access fees generate revenue; discarding would get rid of material.','By selling advertising around previously unpaid broadcasts, the station is _____ its programming. The change concerns generating income from existing content rather than altering the programs’ subjects or their original creators.','Advertising turns programs into revenue sources; disguising concerns concealment.');
add3('neglect','fail to give necessary attention to','neglected details go unattended.','scrutinize,prioritize,corroborate','Analysts who _____ maintenance costs may seriously underestimate the system’s total expense. Those costs require attention alongside the purchase price, yet earlier reports omitted them from every calculation.','Omitting necessary costs indicates lack of attention; prioritize would give them importance.','The editors must not _____ the smaller archive merely because the main collection is larger. Its uncataloged letters also require inspection, and overlooking them could leave relevant evidence unexamined.','Overlooking needed inspection means neglect; scrutinize would examine carefully.');
add3('notional','existing as a concept rather than an actual instance','notional designs exist on paper before reality.','empirical,tangible,substantiated','The plan describes a _____ settlement used to illustrate planning principles; no such town has been built. Its assumed population and layout are conceptual tools rather than observations of an existing place.','Imagined conceptual settlement fits; empirical would be based on observations.','The model assigns a _____ budget to the hypothetical agency, not funds actually appropriated by any government. This imagined amount allows comparisons without asserting that a real allocation exists.','Conceptual assumed budget fits; tangible implies concrete existence.');
add3('obsolete','no longer useful or current','obsolete tools have lost their practical place.','efficacious,novel,indispensable','The software cannot read current file formats or connect to modern equipment. It has become _____ for the laboratory’s work, having lost the usefulness that once made it standard practice.','Loss of usefulness in current work fits; indispensable would mean essential.','The regulation refers exclusively to a technology no longer used anywhere in the industry. Officials call it _____, noting that its requirements no longer address any present operational need.','No present application establishes obsolete; novel means new.');
add3('onerous','burdensome or demanding considerable effort','onerous duties weigh heavily on those performing them.','negligible,optional,effortless','The contract requires hundreds of documented checks each week and extensive reporting after every minor adjustment. Staff describe these _____ obligations as burdensome, consuming time needed for the actual research.','Heavy reporting burden fits; optional would not be compulsory.','Obtaining permission involves repeated travel, lengthy hearings, and costly paperwork. The _____ process places a substantial burden on applicants even when their proposals satisfy every stated eligibility requirement.','Time and cost establish burden; effortless contradicts the described work.');
add3('outmoded','no longer suited to current practice or standards','outmoded fashions belong to an earlier mode.','novel,efficacious,ubiquitous','The handbook assumes that all correspondence travels by post and offers no guidance for digital records. Its _____ procedures reflect an earlier working environment rather than the conditions staff now encounter.','Procedures no longer suit current environment; novel means new.','The design relies on conventions abandoned by the profession decades ago because newer methods better meet current needs. Reviewers call its approach _____ rather than an innovative response to contemporary constraints.','Superseded conventions establish outmoded; efficacious would achieve current goals.');
add3('palpable','so evident that it seems almost tangible','palpable tension feels present in the room.','latent,negligible,equivocal','When the result was announced, the audience fell silent and participants visibly tightened their posture. The tension was _____, unmistakably evident in behavior rather than merely inferred from a private concern.','Unmistakably evident tension fits; latent would be present but unexpressed.','The visitors’ excitement was _____ as they hurried between displays and exclaimed over each discovery. Their enthusiasm was immediately perceptible, not a subtle attitude requiring careful interpretation of uncertain clues.','Openly perceptible excitement fits; equivocal would be ambiguous.');
add3('periodical','a publication issued at regular intervals','periodicals return on a schedule.','monograph,transcript,inventory','The archive subscribed to a _____ that issued a new volume every month, each containing fresh essays and reviews. It was a continuing scheduled publication rather than one self-contained book.','Regular new issues establish periodical; monograph is a single sustained work.','Researchers traced the debate through a _____ published quarterly for two decades. Its successive issues documented changing arguments over time, unlike the single commemorative volume released after the controversy ended.','Quarterly successive issues fit; transcript is a written record of speech.');
add3('perturbation','a disturbance that changes a system’s state','perturbations push a system away from its usual condition.','equilibrium,restoration,uniformity','A brief temperature spike pushed the system away from its stable pattern before it recovered. Researchers measured this _____ to determine how the system responded to a temporary disturbance.','Spike disturbs stable state; equilibrium would describe balance.','The sudden influx of water was a _____ to the normally steady flow, altering pressure throughout the network. Once the disturbance passed, the earlier pattern gradually returned without structural changes.','Influx disturbs usual flow; uniformity means sameness.');
add3('portentous','suggesting that something serious or ominous may follow','portentous signs hint at troubling developments.','jocular,innocuous,irrelevant','The narrator describes darkening skies and distant cracks before the disaster occurs. These _____ details foreshadow danger, giving readers an ominous sense that a consequential event is approaching.','Ominous foreshadowing fits; innocuous would imply harmlessness.','In the chronicle, the sudden silence preceding the army’s arrival carries _____ significance. It functions as an ominous warning of approaching conflict rather than an ordinary observation about background sound.','Warning of serious conflict fits; irrelevant would have no bearing on events.');
add3('predicated','based or founded on a premise','predicated on means resting on an assumption.','contradicted,concealed,substituted','The forecast is _____ on the assumption that demand remains steady. If that premise fails, the projected totals no longer follow, because the entire calculation rests on this particular condition.','Forecast rests on assumption; substituted would mean put in place of it.','The historian’s argument is _____ on the accuracy of the dated ledger, which supplies its foundational chronology. Correcting that document would require rebuilding the causal sequence rather than adjusting a peripheral detail.','Ledger is foundational basis; contradicted would imply conflict with it.');
add3('preempt','act before something occurs to prevent or forestall it','preempting addresses a problem before it begins.','exacerbate,corroborate,elaborate','The team hopes to _____ complaints by explaining the limitations before releasing the results. Its advance disclosure is designed to forestall misunderstandings rather than answer objections after they have already spread.','Advance action forestalls complaints; exacerbate would worsen them.','Officials introduced safeguards to _____ a shortage, increasing reserves while supplies were still adequate. The intervention aimed to prevent the anticipated problem rather than repair damage after resources had run out.','Preventive action precedes shortage; elaborate would add detail.');
add3('prevalent','widespread or commonly occurring','prevalent practices occur across many cases.','sporadic,esoteric,negligible','The spelling appears in most manuscripts from the region, not merely a few unusual examples. It was _____ during that period, although other forms continued to occur in a minority of records.','Majority occurrence establishes widespread use; sporadic would be occasional.','The survey found that the practice was _____ across the profession, with a large majority of respondents reporting regular use. It was therefore a common approach rather than an isolated innovation.','Widespread regular use fits; esoteric implies restricted specialist knowledge rather than frequency.');
add3('proliferate','increase rapidly in number','proliferating examples multiply quickly.','dwindle,disappear,stagnate','New branches _____ after the policy change, increasing from six to more than a hundred within a year. The organization’s presence expands through rapid multiplication of sites rather than larger individual offices.','Rapid numerical multiplication fits; stagnate would mean no growth.','Unverified versions of the story _____ online, with dozens appearing each day where only one existed a week earlier. The rapid increase makes tracking their separate origins increasingly difficult.','Many new versions rapidly appear; dwindle means decrease.');
add3('proponents','people who advocate or support a position','proponents propose and defend a cause.','opponents,observers,beneficiaries','The policy’s _____ publicly defend its provisions and urge the committee to adopt them. Their defining role is active support, regardless of whether they personally receive any benefit from implementation.','Defending adoption establishes supporters; beneficiaries need only receive benefits.','The interpretation has several _____ who argue for its acceptance in articles and lectures. They support its central claims rather than merely describing the debate without taking a position.','Advocacy defines proponents; observers need not support a side.');
add3('proxy','a substitute used to represent something else','a proxy stands in for a harder-to-observe target.','original,obstacle,surplus','Because direct income records were unavailable, researchers used household purchases as a _____ for economic resources. This indirect measure represented the target variable rather than being identical to it.','Indirect stand-in establishes proxy; original would be the actual target.','The analyst uses reported attendance as a _____ for public interest, acknowledging that it imperfectly represents an attitude that cannot be observed directly. The measure stands in for the underlying quantity.','Attendance represents underlying interest; obstacle would impede measurement.');
add3('recapitulate','summarize the main points again','recapitulation returns to the essentials.','repudiate,obscure,augment','At the end of the lecture, the speaker will _____ the three central claims without introducing new material. This brief return helps listeners recall the argument’s structure before questions begin.','Brief return to main claims establishes summary; augment would add material.','The conclusion is intended to _____ the findings, restating their essential results in a compact form. Readers seeking every calculation must consult earlier sections rather than expect full detail here.','Compact restatement summarizes essentials; obscure would reduce clarity.');
add3('regale','entertain with lively accounts or stories','regale an audience by telling engaging tales.','admonish,denigrate,interrogate','The traveler would _____ guests with animated accounts of unusual encounters, making the evening lively through storytelling. Her purpose was to entertain them, not offer instruction or demand answers.','Entertaining stories establish regale; admonish would warn or scold.','At reunions, the researcher likes to _____ former colleagues with amusing stories from early expeditions. Listeners gather for the enjoyable narration rather than a formal report of scientific results.','Amusing narration entertains listeners; interrogate would question them.');
add3('reiterate','state or express again','reiteration repeats an existing statement.','repudiate,obscure,supplant','The revised report will _____ the original warning, stating it again because readers overlooked its first appearance. The authors have not changed their position or introduced a different recommendation.','Same warning stated again indicates repetition; supplant would replace it.','Before closing the meeting, the chair chose to _____ the agreed deadline so everyone heard it a second time. Her final reminder repeated the date announced at the beginning.','Second statement of same deadline fits; repudiate would reject it.');
add3('reprisal','retaliation for a perceived wrong','reprisals strike back at an earlier action.','reconciliation,compensation,disclosure','After the city restricted its exports, the neighboring government imposed new fees in _____. Officials explicitly presented the measure as retaliation for the earlier restriction rather than an unrelated budget decision.','Declared retaliation establishes reprisal; compensation would repay a loss.','The manager reassigned the employee to undesirable duties as a _____ for publicly criticizing the policy. The account describes punishment in response to an earlier action, not a routine staffing change.','Punitive response to criticism indicates retaliation; reconciliation would restore relations.');
add3('restitution','restoration of something lost or wrongfully taken','restitution returns what should have remained yours.','confiscation,reprisal,disclosure','The court ordered _____ of the confiscated artifacts to their lawful owners. Its decision required returning the objects themselves rather than imposing a new penalty or merely publishing their provenance.','Returning wrongfully held objects establishes restitution; confiscation takes possession.','Following the unauthorized withdrawal, the institution made _____ by restoring the missing money to the account. The action returned the original amount rather than offering only an apology for its removal.','Restoration of removed money fits; reprisal would retaliate.');
add3('rudimentary','basic and not highly developed','rudimentary tools supply only the beginnings.','elaborate,comprehensive,esoteric','The first device performed only one simple measurement and lacked the refinements of later models. Its _____ design provided a basic starting point rather than a sophisticated range of capabilities.','Basic undeveloped capabilities fit; comprehensive would cover a broad range.','The student possessed only _____ knowledge of the notation, recognizing its simplest symbols but unable to follow advanced calculations. Her understanding was elementary rather than specialized or extensively developed.','Elementary knowledge of simplest symbols fits; esoteric means restricted specialist knowledge.');
add3('sanction','official approval; a penalty imposed to enforce a rule','context distinguishes permission from punishment.','objection,exemption,acknowledgment','The excavation proceeded with the board’s _____, meaning its formal authorization rather than a private expression of support. A signed permit established official permission after every safety requirement had been satisfied.','Formal authorization and a permit establish approval; acknowledgment recognizes a fact without granting permission.','After repeated violations, the agency imposed a _____ that suspended the operator’s license for six months. This punitive measure enforced the rule rather than approving the conduct or releasing the operator from compliance.','Punitive suspension establishes an enforcement penalty; exemption would release someone from a requirement.');
add3('sincerity','genuineness of expressed feelings or intentions','sincerity means the words match the intent.','fabrication,evasion,hostility','Private letters express the same concern as the public appeal, with no evidence of a hidden agenda. They support the author’s _____ by showing that her stated intentions were genuinely held.','Matching private and public concern supports genuineness; fabrication would be invented fact.','The witness’s actions consistently matched his promises, even when nobody was watching. Colleagues cited this correspondence as evidence of his _____ rather than a performance designed solely to impress an audience.','Actions matching promises demonstrate genuine intent; evasion would avoid responsibility.');
add3('substantial','considerable in amount or extent','substantial gains have meaningful size.','negligible,nonexistent,sporadic','The grant funded most of the repairs and purchased all essential equipment, covering eighty percent of the total cost. Its contribution was _____ rather than a token addition to the budget.','Eighty percent is considerable; negligible would be insignificant.','The new method reduced processing time by nearly half across repeated trials. Researchers described the improvement as _____, emphasizing its considerable magnitude rather than merely noting that any change occurred.','Nearly halving time establishes considerable size; sporadic concerns irregular occurrence.');
add3('succession','a series following one after another','succession puts events in sequence.','simultaneity,stagnation,uniformity','The diary records a _____ of storms, each beginning shortly after the preceding one ended. It presents events occurring one after another rather than one uninterrupted storm or several simultaneous disturbances.','Sequential events establish succession; simultaneity would mean same-time occurrence.','A _____ of editors supervised the journal over its first century, with each taking office after a predecessor departed. Their service formed a chronological series rather than a single collective administration.','Editors follow one another; uniformity concerns sameness, not sequence.');
add3('tally','count or calculate a total','a tally adds separate counts into a total.','estimate,conceal,disregard','The clerks will _____ every recorded vote to determine the exact total. They must count individual entries rather than infer an approximate result from a sample of the submitted ballots.','Exact counting defines tally; estimate would approximate.','Researchers _____ the observations in each category by counting all verified records. Their totals include every qualifying instance rather than a prediction based on how often the event usually occurs.','Complete counting establishes tally; disregard would ignore observations.');
add3('tentative','provisional and subject to revision','tentative conclusions leave room for new evidence.','unequivocal,immutable,irrefutable','The attribution remains _____ because several documents are still unexamined and may change the conclusion. Researchers present it as a provisional judgment rather than a firmly settled identification of the author.','Possible revision establishes provisional status; unequivocal would be unambiguous.','The team offered a _____ explanation while awaiting measurements that could support or contradict it. Their account was explicitly subject to revision once stronger evidence became available from the next experiment.','Awaited potentially contradictory evidence fits provisional; irrefutable would be impossible to disprove.');
add3('tolerance for','capacity to endure something without serious adverse effects','tolerance for stress means enduring it.','dependence on,aversion to,awareness of','The plants’ high _____ drought allows them to survive long dry periods without damage. This capacity concerns enduring water shortage, not requiring it or detecting when rainfall becomes scarce.','Survival without damage establishes endurance capacity; dependence on would imply needing drought.','The material’s limited _____ heat means that temperatures above the threshold quickly weaken its structure. The phrase describes how much stress it can withstand before suffering adverse effects.','Withstanding heat before damage defines tolerance; awareness of implies detection.');
add3('typify','serve as a characteristic example of','typical examples typify a pattern.','contradict,obscure,supplant','These paintings _____ the movement through features found in most of its works: simplified forms, flat color, and deliberate asymmetry. They serve as representative examples rather than unusual exceptions to its conventions.','Shared characteristic features establish representation; contradict would oppose conventions.','The case will _____ the broader pattern because its sequence matches that of most documented instances. Researchers chose it as an illustrative example, not as an anomaly requiring a separate explanation.','Representative pattern-matching example fits; supplant would replace the pattern.');
add3('unprecedented','without an earlier known equivalent','unprecedented events have no known precedent.','recurrent,orthodox,provisional','The archive records no earlier event of comparable scale across its entire documented history. Researchers call this occurrence _____, emphasizing the absence of a known precedent rather than predicting what might happen again.','No earlier equivalent fits; recurrent would mean repeatedly occurring.','For the first time in the institution’s recorded history, every department adopted the same reform simultaneously. This _____ agreement had no earlier counterpart in the extensive records examined by historians.','First known counterpart-free event establishes unprecedented; orthodox means accepted convention.');
add3('vacillate','waver between alternatives','vacillation swings from one choice to another.','persist,converge,comply','The committee members _____ between the two plans, favoring one at breakfast and the other by evening. Their repeated wavering prevents a final choice despite the absence of new evidence.','Repeated changing preference establishes wavering; persist would maintain a course.','Unable to settle on a chronology, the editor continued to _____, repeatedly switching between competing dates. The revisions reflect indecision rather than a stable judgment supported by newly discovered documents.','Switching choices reflects indecision; converge would approach a common point.');
add3('vie','compete for something','rivals vie for the same opportunity.','cooperate,withdraw,concede','Several institutions _____ for the single grant, each trying to secure funding that only one applicant can receive. Their efforts place them in competition rather than a joint proposal for shared support.','Pursuit of exclusive grant establishes competition; cooperate would imply joint effort.','The two interpretations _____ for acceptance among scholars, with advocates seeking support for incompatible accounts. Their rivalry centers on which explanation will become the field’s preferred reading of the evidence.','Rivalry for acceptance means compete; withdraw would abandon pursuit.');
add3('warranted','justified by sufficient reasons or evidence','warranted conclusions have adequate support.','prohibited,anticipated,arbitrary','The conclusion is _____ by several independently verified measurements that exclude the competing explanations. Researchers therefore regard it as justified by evidence rather than a judgment based only on preference or expectation.','Verified exclusion of alternatives supplies justification; anticipated merely means expected.','Given the confirmed structural damage, closing the gallery was _____. The decision rested on a documented safety risk sufficient to justify immediate action rather than on an unsupported fear of possible trouble.','Documented serious risk justifies closure; arbitrary would lack consistent reason.');
